# Forms and validation

- State file rules before the user fails: JPG, JPEG, PNG, PDF, and the size limit.
- Validate as soon as files are chosen. Keep valid files; reject the rest with a clear reason.
- Put errors next to the upload area. Use text, not color alone.
- Keep selected images if some files fail. Do not wipe the whole selection.
- Use human-readable messages. Never show raw MIME types or stack traces.

Allowed formats: JPG, JPEG, PNG, and PDF. Reject DOC, DOCX, TXT, and other types.
Accept PDFs only when the `.pdf` extension, `application/pdf` MIME type, and `%PDF-` file signature agree. Apply the same per-file, total-size, and file-count limits as images; the backend must repeat validation because browser checks are not a trust boundary.

```text
❌ application/pdf is not in ALLOWED_MIME
✅ This file is not a valid PDF document.
```

- Labels must describe the control. Icon-only buttons need an accessible name (for example, “Remove lab-report.png”).
- The Analyze action stays disabled or shows a clear error when nothing is selected.
